    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix two test isolation and concurrency races in `vllm-chat`: a `tracing_core` callsite registration race in `audio_pipeline_attributes_stage_timings_to_request` when run in isolation, and concurrent HF Hub cache lock contention between `roundtrip_gemma4` and `roundtrip_gemma4_hf`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Warms up the multimodal audio pipeline callsites (`vllm.mm.fetch`, `vllm.mm.decode`, `vllm.mm.preprocess`, `vllm.mm.placeholders`) before entering `.with_subscriber(subscriber)` in `audio_pipeline_attributes_stage_timings_to_request`, ensuring the test passes both in isolation and in the full test binary.\n- Adds `#[file_serial(hf_gemma4)]` to `gemma4_hf` in `rust/src/chat/tests/roundtrip.rs` to match `roundtrip_gemma4` (which shares the `google/gemma-4-E4B-it` HF Hub cache lock and test vector generation), and removes a stale `#[allow(dead_code)]` attribute on `kimi_k25`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- **Reproducer (without fix vs with fix):**\n  - Without fix: Running `cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p vllm-chat --lib --locked -- audio_pipeline_attributes_stage_timings_to_request` in isolation fails (`assertion failed: timing.placeholders_s > 0.0`), and running `roundtrip_gemma4` + `roundtrip_gemma4_hf` concurrently with an unpopulated cache fails with `Lock file \".../models--google--gemma-4-E4B-it/.locks/...\" is already owned by the current process`.\n  - With fix: Both pass deterministically in isolation and in parallel.\n- **Test commands run:**\n  ```bash\n  cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p vllm-chat --lib --locked -- audio_pipeline_attributes_stage_timings_to_request\n  cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p vllm-chat --lib --locked -- audio::tests\n  cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml -p vllm-chat --test roundtrip --locked -- roundtrip_gemma4\n  cargo fmt --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --all -- --check\n  cargo clippy --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings\n  ```\n- **Results:** `1 passed; 0 failed` in isolation, `10 passed; 0 failed` in `audio::tests`, `2 passed; 0 failed` in `roundtrip_gemma4*`, and zero `cargo fmt` / `cargo clippy` warnings.\n- **Model evaluation:** N/A (test-only reliability fixes in `vllm-chat`).\n\n## Details\n\n- **Root cause:**\n  1. `tracing::instrument::WithSubscriber` installs a thread-local default subscriber via `tracing::dispatcher::with_default` as the future is polled on Tokio worker threads. When `with_default` rebuilds `tracing_core` callsite interest caches, only callsites that have already executed at least once are registered in the global callsite list; callsites reached for the first time after a worker thread polls the future can retain `Interest::never()` when no global subscriber is installed. Warming up `info.prepare_multimodal(...)` once before `.with_subscriber(subscriber)` registers all four stage callsites beforehand.\n  2. `roundtrip_gemma4` had `#[file_serial(hf_gemma4)]`, whereas `roundtrip_gemma4_hf` resolved and wrote test vectors for the same `google/gemma-4-E4B-it` model without `#[file_serial(hf_gemma4)]`.\n- **Duplicate-PR check:** Searched open PRs via `gh pr list --repo vllm-project/vllm --state open --search \"audio_pipeline_attributes_stage_timings_to_request OR gemma4_hf\"`; no existing PR addresses these test races.\n- **AI assistance:** AI assistance was used to diagnose the test races and prepare this PR; all changes were reviewed and verified locally.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resour